{'symbol': 'ORCL', 'date': '2021-06-30 08:00:00', 'title': 'ORACLE CLOUD INFRASTRUCTURE GAINS APPROVAL FOR MORE GOVERNMENT WORKLOADS', 'text': 'AUSTIN, TEXAS, JUNE 30, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0WITH NEW AUTHORIZATIONS, ORACLE IS MAKING MORE CLOUD SERVICES AVAILABLE TO CUSTOMERS IN ITS US GOVERNMENT REGIONS.\xa0SPECIFICALLY, ORACLE HAS ATTAINED FEDRAMP\xa0HIGH PROVISIONAL AUTHORITY TO OPERATE (P-ATO) FROM THE JOINT AUTHORIZATION BOARD (JAB) AND DEFENSE INFORMATION SYSTEMS AGENCY\xa0(DISA) IMPACT LEVEL 5 (IL5) ACCREDITATION FOR IAAS AND PAAS, WHICH INCLUDE AN EXTENDED SET OF CLOUD SERVICES FOR GOVERNMENT CUSTOMERS TO LEVERAGE, INCLUDING ORACLE DIGITAL ASSISTANT\xa0AND ORACLE CLOUD VMWARE SOLUTION, TO BOOST EFFICIENCY WITHOUT STRAINING BUDGETS OR COMPROMISING SECURITY.'}